Unit 3. Memory Listen to Soe Thu talking about his childhood events.

g11-audio-3-2
00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:18.910
I don't have a very good memory, but sometimes, certain sights, smells, tastes or even sounds make me remember some of my childhood events.

g11-audio-3-3
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:27.050
For example, the smell and taste of mohinga always remind me of my mother because she used to cook mohinga on Sundays when we were young.

g11-audio-3-4
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:32.230
And whenever I hear the song You Are My Sunshine, it makes me think of my neighbor friend,

g11-audio-3-5
00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:32.870
Cho Cho.

g11-audio-3-6
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.890
We liked the song so much that we often sang it on the way back home after school.

g11-audio-3-7
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.650
Another thing is that when I see a white cat with black spots, it reminds me of my first pet cat.

g11-audio-3-8
00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.670
She was called Mi Phyu and I still remember the day I got her.

g11-audio-3-9
00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.850
It was my seventh birthday.

g11-audio-3-10
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.990
I was really excited as she was so cute.

g11-audio-3-11
00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.230
She used to sit by my side while I was studying and I played with her before I went to bed.
